In the TV show Dexter, Dexter originally starts dating his girlfriend as a cover for his secret life as a
serial killer; however, as the show progresses, he quickly begins to truly love her and her kids, which
interferes with his night life negatively. Eventually, though, he decides to marry her and have a child with
her.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

In Dexter, a colleague named Doakes dedicates all of his time and even sacrifices his job on discovering
Dexter's secret. Eventually, Doakes find irrefutable proof that Dexter is the Bay Harbor Butcher, and when
Dexter discovers this, he kidnaps Doakes and holds him hostage in a cabin in the woods. Knowing that he can
not keep Doakes captive forever, though, Dexter thinks about what he can do with Doakes to permanently solve
this problem. Dexter realizes, however, that his only options are to kill Doakes or to release him, or to
turn himself in. Dexter establishes his entire identity on a code given to him by his father, with the first rule being to not get
rule being to not get caught, which rules out turning himself in; however, the code also importantly states
never to murder an innocent person, which Doakes is, and releasing Doakes would result in Dexter getting
arrested regardless.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Dexter woke up one day, this day initially being no different from any other in the 15 years he worked at
Miamo Metro Police Department. However, when he arrived at his lab, he saw a new man there, who was placing
his belongings on his desk. When Dexter saw this, he approached his long-time friend Angel and asked him who
the new man was. "James Doakes," Angel replied, "He's ex-special ops. No one knows why he was transferred
here though." Dexter thanked Angel and returned to his lab, constantly keeping an eye on Doakes to determine
if he will be a threat to Dexter's secret life as the Bay Harbor Butcher. The next few months proceed as
they always had, until one day during a crime scene investigation, Doakes began to realize how excited
Dexter gets when describing crime scenes, and how Dexter acts around people as if it's all an act. Meanwhile,
Miami Metro is hunting the Ice Truck Killer, the only currently known serial killer in Miami. In secret,
Doakes stalks Dexter at night in an attempt to find what he is hiding, for Doakes knows that Dexter is
connected to the Ice Truck Killer because of his many unexplainable interactions with the Ice Truck Killer.
Unaware of what Doakes is doing, Dexter kidnaps a serial pedophile and sets up his kill room in a secluded building.
Doakes is following him, though, and immediately before Dexter plunges his glistening knife into the man's
heart, Doakes interrupts Dexter, gun in hand, telling Dexter to surrender. Dexter pretends to surrender, but
when Doakes approaches him to handcuff him, Dexter fights back, overpowering Doakes, injects him with M99,
and puts him in his vehicle. Putting his current kill on hold, Dexter drives to an abandoned cabin in the
woods, sets up a steel cage, and locks Doakes in it. Dexter then returns to his kill room to finish the
kill, and returns to his cabin. By this time, Doakes is awake and begins to talk to Dexter, trying to
convince him to turn himself in, or to let him go. Dexter initally wants to kill Doakes as an easy solution,
but it would break his father's code which states that Dexter should never kill an innocent person, which
Doakes is. "The first rule of the code is to never get caught." Dexter thought to himself nervously, unsure
of what he could do. Ultimately, Dexter decides to make the Bay Harbor Butcher's existence known to Miami
Metro, and to frame Doakes as the Bay Harbor Butcher, releasing Doakes afterward for the justice system to
handle.